The library module lends books to students, teachers and staff from the same application you already
use. It keeps a catalogue of titles, one record per physical copy, who has borrowed what, holds,
fines, stock-takes and reports. Borrowers are the people already on your records: nobody is entered
twice.

> The Library is a recent addition and may not be switched on for your institute yet. If you do not
> see **Library** in the drawer, ask your administrator to grant a role access to it.

## How lending works

- **Copies carry a barcode.** Every physical book has a label. Scanning it identifies the copy.
- **People are identified by their ID card.** The number on a student's or teacher's card is their
  RFID, the same number attendance uses. Tapping the card on a USB reader at the desk opens that
  person. See [Issue and Replace ID Cards](/docs/educonnect-tutorial-id-cards).
- **Both devices act as a keyboard.** The desk needs no extra software, and a phone or laptop camera
  can scan instead of a handheld scanner. See [The Circulation Desk](/docs/educonnect-library-circulation-desk).

## The Library drawer

| Screen | What it is for | Guide |
| --- | --- | --- |
| **Circulation Desk** | Lend, return, renew | [Circulation Desk](/docs/educonnect-library-circulation-desk) |
| **Catalogue** | Books and copies, import, labels | [Catalogue](/docs/educonnect-library-catalogue) |
| **Loans & Overdue** | Everything out, what is late, what came back today | [Circulation Desk](/docs/educonnect-library-circulation-desk) |
| **Holds** | The hold shelf and reservation queues | [Holds](/docs/educonnect-library-holds) |
| **Borrowers** | Each person's loans, holds, fines and limits | [Borrowers](/docs/educonnect-library-borrowers) |
| **Fines** | Unpaid, paid and waived library fines | [Fines](/docs/educonnect-library-fines) |
| **Stock-take** | Check the shelves against the catalogue | [Stock-take](/docs/educonnect-library-stocktake) |
| **Reports** | Circulation, collection and fines figures | [Reports](/docs/educonnect-library-reports) |
| **Library Settings** | Loan rules, fines, holds, labels, portal | below |

Teachers who have been granted it also see **My Library**. See
[My Library](/docs/educonnect-library-my-library).

## Who can do what

Everything is controlled in **Access Control**, under the **Library** group. There is a ready-made
**librarian** role. It lands on the Circulation Desk and holds the desk, holds, borrowers, catalogue,
stock-take, fines, waiving fines and reports. It does **not** include **Library settings**, which
stay with the administrator until you grant them.

The main permissions:

| Permission | Allows |
| --- | --- |
| Search the catalogue | View books and availability |
| Circulation desk | Open the desk, loans and borrowers |
| Check out & renew / Check in returns | Lend and take back |
| Override borrowing limits, blocks & holds | Lend past a limit or block, with a reason |
| Add & edit books and copies; Withdraw, repair & restore | Maintain the catalogue |
| Bulk import the catalogue | Spreadsheet import |
| Start a stock-take; Finalise | Run and close a stock-take |
| Declare books lost & charge damage | Assess fines |
| Waive unpaid library fines | A money decision, so it is separate from the fines group |
| Library reports | View reports |
| Library settings | Change the rules below |

Teachers get **no** library permissions by default. Tick them on when your library goes live.

## Library Settings

Open **Library → Library Settings** (needs the settings permission).

- **Loan rules**: separately for students, teachers and staff: books at a time (0 means that type
  cannot borrow), loan length in days, renewals and days per renewal. Defaults: students 2 books for
  14 days; teachers 10 for 30; staff 5 for 30.
- **Move due dates off closed days**: a due date on a weekend, holiday or outside term moves to the
  next school day.
- **No new books while one is overdue**.
- **Circulation desk**: close the borrower after a set number of seconds without a scan (default 90),
  so the next child's books never land on the previous child's card; and **Lend only on a card tap**,
  which makes looking someone up by name need an override.
- **Charge library fines**: see [Fines](/docs/educonnect-library-fines). Off until you opt in.
- **Holds**: whether borrowers can reserve, holds per borrower, and school days to collect.
- **Parent portal**: show the library to parents, let them reserve, let them pay fines online.
- **Overdue reminders**: a weekly push at 7 am to every borrower with an overdue book (a student's
  parents, or the teacher). Off by default.
- **ISBN lookup**: adds a **Look up** button to the add-book form. It sends the ISBN to Open Library,
  so it is off until you opt in.
- **Barcode labels**: the **Label prefix** (default `LIB`, giving `LIB000001`, `LIB000002` and so
  on). Labels already printed keep their number, so choose a distinct prefix if books may move
  between campuses.
- **Shelf locations**: the vocabulary offered when adding copies, for example "Fiction A–F".

## Not in this version

Teachers and staff are never fined, and there is no separate search service: catalogue search matches
the start of words in titles, authors and similar fields.
